Z||000000||bHooper||08-20-99||10:18 PM||||I would like to know anyones thoughts about <br>the Y2K problem and the Fiero.  Will this cause any problems with the computer in the cars on 1/1/00?
Z||000001||Cooter||08-20-99||10:51 PM||||We have addressed this subject before and came to the conclusion that your car's computer doesn't give a rat's butt what time, day or date it is. Just out of curiosity, I set the on board display/computer in my dad's 88 Reatta to 12/31/99 and watched it click over to the year 2000 and the car still runs. I think we are safe. As bad of time keepers as computers are (especially those from the mid 80's), there would already be cars suffering from the "bug" because their clocks had run fast enough ahead to already think it was 2000. Besides, its not like you will have anywhere to go on 1/1/00- everything is going to shutdown anyway, right????? (just kidding)
